#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:12
msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:14
msgid ""
"This controller is a class compliant USB MIDI and audio device, so it can be"
" used without any special drivers on GNU/Linux, Mac OS X, and Windows. "
"However, if you wish to use the [ASIO sound "
"API](https://mixxx.org/manual/latest/chapters/preferences/sound_hardware.html?highlight=asio#windows)"
" under Windows, please install the latest driver package available from the "
"[Support "
"page](https://support.hercules.com/en/product/djcontrolinpulse200-en//)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:16
msgid "Sound Card Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:18
msgid ""
"This controller has built-in 4 channel output sound card, with "
"{hwlabel}`MASTER` output (RCA) and {hwlabel}`HEADPHONE` output (3.5mm jack)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:20
msgid "Open {guilabel}`Preferences > Sound Hardware`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:21
msgid "Select the {guilabel}`Output` tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:22
msgid ""
"From the {guilabel}`Main` drop-down menu, select the audio interface, then "
"{guilabel}`Channels 1 - 2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:23
msgid ""
"From the {guilabel}`Headphones` drop-down menu, select the audio interface, "
"then {guilabel}`Channels 3 - 4`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:24
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Apply` to save the changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:27
msgid ""
"The {ref}`example setups section <setup-laptop-and-external-card>` provides "
"more details about the audio configuration in Mixxx."
msgstr ""

#: ../../hardware/controllers/hercules_djcontrol_inpulse_200.md:31
msgid ""
"The {hwlabel}`MASTER` and {hwlabel}`HEADPHONE` knobs, as well as the    "
"{hwlabel}`MASTER` button are hardware controls and interact directly with "
"the    integrated sound card’s output. Although they also send MIDI "
"messages,    they have NOT been mapped in Mixxx, so do not expect an on-"
"screen    reaction when using them. This was done to prevent the knobs to "
"adjust    both the gain on the controller’s sound card and in Mixxx."
msgstr ""

